1.1.0 2026-10-14
  - Regenerated all BIDS recordings with the corrected MOABB Rozado2015 loader
    (https://github.com/NeuroTechX/moabb/pull/1260, issue
    https://github.com/NeuroTechX/moabb/issues/1070).
    Channel 0 of the XDF EEG stream is the trigger (Trig1). Versions up to
    1.0.2 took the first 32 channels by position: the channel labelled Fp1
    held the (constant) trigger, every other label was shifted by one
    electrode (the data labelled AF3 was Fp1, ..., the data labelled Cz was
    Fz) and Cz was missing. Channels are now picked by label. The stream's
    declared microvolts were also scaled as raw ADC counts (x 31.25e-9
    instead of x 1e-6), so EEG amplitudes were 32 times too small; they are
    now scaled correctly. Sampling rate (512 Hz), events (1,550) and the list
    of recordings are unchanged; the BAD_ACQ_SKIP annotation and the extra
    padding second at the end of the old BDF files are gone.
  - derivatives/neural_signatures regenerated from the corrected recordings.
  - README regenerated from the corrected loader metadata;
    code/Rozado2015.metadata.yaml updated.
  - sourcedata/ unchanged.
